00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.000
And then, the day came. 

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:21.000
It had been a bright, sunny day. The sun was setting, huge against the orange sky. The forest sounds were getting quieter, ready for the night. 

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:37.000
I looked around me: I tried to memorise the colours, the smells of my homeland, I packed them all in my brain, I stored them safely to keep myself warm during my journey. 

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:44.000
I looked at my mother’s eyes. She was proud. She was terrified. 

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:50.000
She had done the journey herself, though she had always refused to talk about it. 

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.000
“I’ll be fine, Ma. Don’t worry.” 

00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:02.000
“Of course you’ll be fine”, she said, then she looked away. She didn’t want me to see her doubt.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.000
I flew to the top of our tree to warm up. 

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:14.500 
I looked at the open sky. It was so huge, you couldn’t see the end of it. I felt dizzy. 

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:25.000
Despite the heat, I started to shiver, my heart pounding in my chest. How could I possibly do this? 

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:37.000
Maybe it was a big mistake. Maybe I wasn’t ready. Maybe I could wait, just a little longer. 

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:46.000
I heard a bird laugh behind me. It was a fat bird of paradise, munching on berries. 

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:51.000
“What’s up with you willow warbler? Having second thoughts?” 

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:55.000
“I’m just stretching my wings, getting ready for the flight, that’s all.” 

00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:02.000
“No kidding. A tiny bird like you, making it to Europe? How much do you weigh? 10g?” 

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:08.000
“8. Still, it’s not the weight that counts, it’s the spirit. 

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:18.000
But how could you understand? Birds of paradise have it easy. Big guns like you take all the food. Come summer, there will be nothing left for us.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:27.000
And predators are getting stronger too, they are just waiting for an opportunity to munch on the little ones too weak to escape. 

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:38.000
So don’t talk to me like I have a choice. Live or die, that’s the only choice we have. And I choose to live.“ 

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:50.000
And then, without another thought, I opened my little green wings and took off.
